## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a safe, production-grade debugging workflow leveraging Time Travel and dbt macros while preserving tenant isolation and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped debug mirroring
- dbt macros for environment toggling
- Snowflake Time Travel for backfills
- CI gating and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro swap_tenant_debug(tenant, mode) -%}
  {% if mode == 'debug' -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_{{tenant}}.debug_hourly_engagement;
  {% else -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_base.hourly_engagement;
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely expire old debug objects?
- How would you audit backfill changes across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a realistic, privacy‑aware multi‑tenant pipeline. Requires macro generation of tenant-scoped models, conditional data masking, and governance hooks (lineage, snapshots) under CI.

## Key Concepts

- dbt macros for tenant-scoped models
- per-tenant privacy rules (PII redaction/hash)
- incremental loading with a 1-day late window
- tests: not_null, unique keys
- snapshots and lineage governance
- CI validation across many tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo macro sketch (dbt uses Jinja in SQL)
{% macro redact_fields(field, privacy_tier) %}
  {% if privacy_tier == 'public' %}
    {{ field }}
  {% else %}
    SHA2({{ field }}, 256)
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor privacy violations in production and adjust masking rules?
- How would you scale testing and CI for 100s of tenants without slowing commits?
